<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Indonesia to import more Australia cattle.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Indonesia to import more Australia cattle.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia has boosted its Australian live cattle export allocations to 407,000 head for 1997, Queensland economic development and trade minister, Doug Slack, said.</p>
<p>&quot;This means that an additional 27,000 head at least will be exported to Indonesia which is Queensland's biggest live cattle market,&quot; Slack said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;I am told this will provide additional income of A$13 million,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>Slack said Indonesia had also announced a 33 percent increase to 30,000 tonnes in imports of Australian chilled and frozen beef, significantly increasing last year's export earnings of A$60 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
